WEBVTT

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.360
What... just happened?

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:16.370
Can it be...

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.510
they sent <i>you</i>?!

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.870
Somenki...

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.540
Are... Are you the one who did this?

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.320
Your request for aid was received.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.920
A few others were sent ahead of me,

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.120
but all were killed.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:42.930
With Sett dead as well, 
it was only natural they sent me.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:50.880
I fail to understand why slaughtering 
a single kingdom of humans proved so difficult.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.450
I let a mere three—no,

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.810
<i>four</i>—humans slip through.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.950
So you're a human now, too.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.290
Somenki...

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:03.490
Damn you!

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.110
Can you fire your cannon?

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.960
Are your muscles as they once were?

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:09.790
What of your <i>xian dao?</i>

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:12.490
And most importantly, 
where is your horn?

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.090
You are a human now.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.100
If you have any pride left, 
you should die with dignity!

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.350
I'll carry out the deed myself!

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.850
You're right.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.250
Kill me if you like—

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.230
Hold it!

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.040
If it's all the same to you, 
why not let us have her?

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.370
Do you realize 
what's going on right now?

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:42.840
You saw Somenki's cannon. 
You should realize how powerful—

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:43.890
Hey, no worries.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.830
We'll be just fine!

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:24.490
Species and Belonging

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.480
Well, Frau, what's the plan?

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:28.430
I'm pretty darn scared right now!

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:32.260
Sally beat that walrus!

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.230
Sally is strong!

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.360
I told you that
I don't remember doing that!

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.360
<i>You</i> killed Sett?

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:41.360
Yes, but I don't remember—

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:41.860
Interesting!

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:44.190
<i>Hold it, Somenki!</i>

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.620
Sumeragi?

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:51.190
Why should I stop?

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.000
<i>Because those are your orders.</i>

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.020
Ogre is talking to someone.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.620
My orders were to kill everyone 
in this region.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.760
<i>Indeed they were.</i>

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.210
<i>But that girl is an exception.</i>

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:06.760
<i>Harming her would have
 irritating consequences.</i>

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.340
<i>What kind of consequences?</i>

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.260
Oh, honestly.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.640
I'll explain when you're back.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:18.390
Just leave them be 
and come back already.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:21.280
These are your orders, as well.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:25.160
Very well.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:43.560
Oh, I was so scared!

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:44.550
There, there.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.340
Give me a break already!

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:52.560
It's just one bit of nonsense after another!

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.260
But...

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:59.320
It really is all gone, isn't it?

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:06.800
Hawthorn!

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.530
I forgot! Hawthorn will be in even
 worse shape than we are!

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:11.760
Hawthorn?

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.910
Hey! You hear me?

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.480
Get a hold of yourself!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.580
Sally...

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:20.760
What's going on?

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:22.620
Am I dreaming?

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:24.620
Hawthorn...

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.430
You've got to get a grip!

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.430
We're out of weapons, 
food, water... everything!

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.190
We have to get moving!

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.710
I know it's a lot to take in.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:39.190
I know that you're confused.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.190
But you have to be strong!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.300
Y-Yeah... Good point.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:48.540
Let's get going to the closest town.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:51.230
Um... where was it again?

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.830
Sorry, my head's still a little fuzzy.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:59.460
There's a city a half-day's walk to the west.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.340
How do you know?

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:06.340
I learned the local terrain 
while preparing our invasion.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.650
I don't have anywhere to go, either.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.680
I might as well help you out for now.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.230
Hey! What are you—

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:17.980
Good girl!

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.370
Let's just go!

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:23.580
Okay!

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:24.790
Hawthorn, can you stand?

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.070
Uh, yeah...

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:36.720
Guess we ought to get an inn.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:38.330
If only we had money...

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.500
I've got some pocket change, at least.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:44.500
Though I doubt they'll rent a room 
to a demihuman.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.510
Don't worry. I'll handle it.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:50.010
You have to be kidding!

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.390
We can't let a demihuman stay here!

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.710
You—

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:57.390
Sir, do you recognize me?

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.650
I'm the regimental commander 
of the Knights of Rimdarl,

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.650
Hawthorn Grattor.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:08.630
Oh, the commander 
who's always here on patrols!

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.400
So you do remember me!

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.040
But...

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.410
What are you doing with a demihuman?

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.620
Is this some kind of mission?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.360
Something like that.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.790
That particular demihuman's harmless.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:22.950
I give you my word.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:24.170
Won't you let us stay?

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:29.880
I just don't get it!

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:32.640
Everyone we meet is such a jerk 
about demihumans!

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.260
It's their upbringing.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.470
They can't help it.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.220
"Upbringing"?

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:40.840
Anyway, here.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.980
Use this to buy us some food for now.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.020
And make every coin count!

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:51.900
Now that I'm unemployed, 
this is all I have in the world.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:54.910
Glad to hear it.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.660
Seems to me 
you're bouncing back a little.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:02.190
Well, I got a slap 
from the invincible Sally.

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:04.040
Who wouldn't be energized?

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:05.390
I see!

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:08.330
Well, I'll be back soon!

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:10.270
Sure thing. Take care!

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.680
What's the matter with you?

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.940
I feel a little pathetic.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:26.190
My "brave face" energy just ran out.

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:30.240
So you were putting on an act 
for that human?

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:33.050
Perfectly understandable.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:35.100
But if you're not careful—

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.720
No, that's not the issue.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:42.110
I'm still a knight. I can accept death.

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.160
But...

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:47.270
The civilians I sought to protect 
by facing death,

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:50.310
the lord I served, my very home...

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.550
The thought of that all being gone...

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.120
Hawthorn.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.310
All will work out probably!

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.490
So cheer up!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.860
Frau...

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:07.100
"Probably"? What in the world?

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:13.860
Honestly... 
I'm not sure I'll ever understand you.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:16.860
Sorry to let myself slip like that.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.340
I'll get us some water downstairs.

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:21.370
I need to cool off.

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:26.120
"Frau," was it?

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:29.130
You're awfully close with these humans.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.880
Are you really a demihuman?

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:35.130
Frau went on a journey.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:38.140
Faced prejudice when alone.

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:42.390
Stones thrown. Carrots stolen.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.440
Frau passed out on the road.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.960
But then Frau met Sally.

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:51.400
Sally was kind.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:54.930
Protected Frau from humans.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.960
And... smiled at Frau.

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:03.660
I wonder what allowed her 
to smile at you—

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:05.960
Because Sally is Sally!

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:09.020
Child should travel with Sally, too!

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:13.790
Well, it's not as if 
I have anywhere else to go.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:17.160
And why are you calling me "child"?

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:19.340
Frau doesn't know child's proper name!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:20.550
That's just humiliating!

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:25.480
And humanoid ogres aren't allowed 
to have their own names!

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:27.560
It's a rule!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:29.810
But what to call, without a name?

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.930
If you insist.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:35.320
You pick one then, Frau.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.380
Carrot (<i>ninjin</i>)?

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:37.200
What?!

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.250
Not good?

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:39.730
Of course not!

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:41.320
At least try to be reasonable!

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:44.700
Carrot (<i>kyarotto</i>)!

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:47.700
"Carrot"...

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:50.660
I suppose that's less awful.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.800
Food for four...

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.220
Not sure I'll have enough.

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:04.260
Now that I'm unemployed, 
this is all I have in the world.

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:09.430
Can I justify continuing my journey like this?

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:15.480
I could call it off and
 take them back to my kingdom.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:20.390
<i>Ogres...</i>

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:21.740
<i>Demihumans...</i>

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:26.290
<i>I never thought about things 
like species and prejudice before.</i>

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:28.750
<i>I want to help, but I can't.</i>

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:32.740
<i>I'm no different from how I was then.</i>

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.250
No, <i>you</i> be reasonable!

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:38.670
At least buy some proper dog food for once!

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:41.200
I can't afford to waste money.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:45.380
Food for your faithful companion is a waste?!

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:46.050
Mi—

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:47.080
Mikoto?

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:49.980
Sally?

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:54.560
<i>I'm so excited!</i>

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.150
<i>I finally found him!</i>

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:59.070
You cut your hair.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.070
Y-Yeah.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.510
It suits you.

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:05.320
I like you better this way.

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.790
Th-Thank you...

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.740
I cut it before I left on my journey.

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:13.210
Sort of a "declaration of intent."

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:17.090
You've been through a lot, haven't you?

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:18.590
Yeah...

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:25.500
I'd never have met so many people 
or been through so many things

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:28.310
if I had stayed as a princess.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.350
And I understand the world 
a little better now.

00:12:31.210 --> 00:12:34.860
But why does "species" matter? 
Why does prejudice exist?

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:40.730
Humans treat harmless demihumans 
with contempt.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:44.610
Ogres are blindly hostile to humans.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:47.710
Nobody even seems to question it.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.010
Here's a hypothetical for you:

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:59.750
Let's say a demihuman kills a human.

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:02.630
How do you think 
that human's child would feel?

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:05.870
Well, they'd be sad at first...

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:07.140
Then what?

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:09.470
I'd hate them.

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:15.270
If I killed the demihuman responsible, 
nobody would question that.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:18.520
But do you think I would stop there?

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:21.020
Certainly not.

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:25.180
If I were strong enough 
to kill a demihuman,

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:31.030
I'd kill them all without hesitation.

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:33.540
M-Mikoto?

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:38.030
All purely hypothetical, of course.

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:39.710
Right...

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:43.650
But prejudice isn't necessarily 
caused by hatred.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.790
It can be a fear born of ignorance,

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:48.270
a discomfort—born from an obsession 
with purity—with the different.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.680
It varies greatly.

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:53.310
So everyone has their own reasons?

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:58.670
No... what most people have 
doesn't even qualify as a "reason."

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:01.820
It's just how they were brought up.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.180
Father!

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.700
What is it, Kenness?

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:11.180
Look!

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:13.080
I baked cookies!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.080
You're so talented, Kenness!

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.000
Share them with everyone, won't you?

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.080
Okay!

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:31.760
Could you kindly not devour 
a man's flock, Somenki?

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.320
And you...

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:38.230
Still keeping up 
the bizarre wandering-priest act,

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:39.400
Sumeragi?

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:43.610
It was a close call, though.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.230
What was?

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:49.700
If I hadn't stopped you, 
that princess would have killed you.

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:53.620
You... Your jokes have grown stale 
since last we met.

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:58.460
My body, granted to me by my creator,

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:00.870
would never fall to a mere human!

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:06.000
A human that could grow 
to the power of a Kishin.

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:09.510
All the more reason to nip it 
in the bud!

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:12.010
Who ordered you to stop me?

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:14.290
The First.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.140
But it's still not right!

00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:21.770
It's not just demihumans.

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:25.900
I've seen other species start 
to understand each other.

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:30.170
The first being I met on my journey 
was a demihuman.

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:34.160
They're a bit strange, 
but they're also really nice.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:42.980
You might be the only person 
in the world who knows that, Sally.

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:46.720
Things only I know...

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:48.940
Things only I can do...

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:53.180
I've decided on a purpose for my journey!

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:57.010
Mikoto! I really hate prejudice!

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:58.680
I <i>really</i> hate it!

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:04.310
So you're going to travel around 
and preach anti-discrimination?

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:08.070
No. That wouldn't do any good.

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:11.820
But... I want to create 
at least a little compromise!

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.280
I think I want that 
to be the purpose of my journey!

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:17.610
It'll be a road covered in thorns.

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:19.200
That's okay!

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:21.510
I can handle a little pain!

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:27.570
A-And... you could join me, if you want.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:28.960
Unfortunately...

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:31.790
I prefer the ease of a solo journey.

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:33.770
I see.

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:35.240
But...

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:38.730
if I keep traveling, 
we might run into each other again, right?

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:40.720
Indeed.

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:44.230
Let's both have lots of stories 
to tell when that happens.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:49.900
Sally.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:53.350
You really have changed.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:06.250
The princess is still watching.

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:08.270
Why not grant her a look back?

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.090
Dog.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:15.760
I expected Sally to say, 
"Take me with you," again.

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:18.290
But she did say that!

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:19.220
No...

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:22.140
She offered to let me join her.

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:26.640
I think if I looked back now, 
I'd end up taking her offer,

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:28.940
so I'm running away instead.

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:39.270
Well, what now?

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:41.020
Captain!

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:43.010
I knew it!

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:45.560
Captain Hawthorn!

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:48.930
You're...

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:53.420
I'm back!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.580
Keep it down.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:55.830
Agreed.

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:56.670
Welcome!

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:59.210
I like Frau best!

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:01.680
Hey, who's that?

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.010
Hawthorn's...

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:03.920
Hawthorn's...

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:05.740
Finish the sentence, darn it!

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:08.690
Don't jump to conclusions!

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:10.690
This is Berett.

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:12.190
He's one of my soldiers.

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:14.440
I said <i>he</i>, by the way.

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:17.450
Oh, he's a boy?

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.450
A pleasure to meet you. 
I'm Sally.

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:23.440
That harefolk is Frau.

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:27.460
And that's... um...

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:31.210
P-Please call me "Carrot."

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:33.600
Carrot?

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:36.840
You needed a name to call me, right?

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:39.110
Frau named!

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:41.610
Hey, I like that!

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:44.720
A pleasure to meet you, Carrot.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:47.630
Hawthorn.

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:50.350
You said that boy was one of your men?

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:51.310
Yeah.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:53.740
He survived the destruction 
of the Kingdom of Rimdarl.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.990
Could you tell Sally 
what you just told me?

00:18:58.460 --> 00:18:59.330
Yes...

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:05.370
I was guarding the library as usual, when...

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:13.880
Wh-Who are you?

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:16.000
How did you get in?!

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:28.610
I thought I was the only one left.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.020
Mom! Dad!

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:34.650
I'll find someone to take you in.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:35.900
Don't worry.

00:19:37.810 --> 00:19:41.610
But who could send him 
to the forest in a flash?

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:46.050
The Witch of the Western Forest, I'll bet.

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:47.540
Witch?!

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:49.730
You know this person?

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:52.920
Yeah, she's a stingy little witch.

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:54.720
A witch...

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:56.250
Magic?

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.400
I want to meet this person!

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:01.180
Huh?!

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:03.450
She saved Berett, right?

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:05.680
So we'd better thank her!

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:11.680
Drifting down the river... Pale crimson...
 A life of ten thousand years...

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:14.650
Its name... a peach.

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:24.990
What are you doing here?

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.240
Oh, Meki!

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.490
I'm so glad you came.

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:33.550
Come to finish the job Somenki started?

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:35.890
Perish the thought!

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:39.150
I came to return you to our side.

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:44.380
For an ogre who's lost its horn 
to still be called an ogre,

00:20:44.690 --> 00:20:48.760
they must retain a great deal of power.

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:55.190
I could perform a service, 
receive power, and return?

00:20:55.740 --> 00:20:57.180
I could be an ogre again?

00:20:57.800 --> 00:20:59.770
What do you want me to do?

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:06.190
Just travel with your little party, 
and report to me what happens.

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:08.030
In other words...

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:10.540
Become your spy?

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:14.050
Nothing so dramatic.

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:15.930
Just keep it simple.

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:17.540
Unless...

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.550
You haven't developed feelings 
for them, have you?

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:22.800
Certainly not!

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:25.700
I see. That's a relief.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:28.780
You can still use your <i>xian dao</i>, 
can't you?

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:31.630
If anything happens, 
send an eye my way.

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:33.300
Oh...

00:21:34.170 --> 00:21:39.810
And try looking at them 
through your <i>xian dao's</i> eyes some time.

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:43.100
Farewell, Meki!

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:47.650
Master Sumeragi!

00:21:47.650 --> 00:21:49.770
I have arrived!

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:53.330
And right on time, Sister Millia!

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:55.080
Yes!

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:57.740
What can I do for you?

00:21:58.090 --> 00:22:00.220
Let's call it... support.

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:02.090
"Support"?

00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:06.630
Now... let's set up a little welcome

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:08.340
for that bitch.

00:22:09.100 --> 00:22:10.220
It's so big!

00:22:10.590 --> 00:22:13.390
Is this where the witch lives?

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:50.250
Companion and Companion

00:23:46.380 --> 00:23:49.230
Next time: "Companion and Companion."
